singer  songwriter do you know icon it's just  not something you ever really imagined  Gord downy along with the hip have been  providing the soundtrack to our lives  since releasing their first EP back in  1987  [Music]  14 studio albums over 8 million albums  sold 16 Juno Awards a star on Canada's  Walk of Fame yet the ban was even  awarded a Governor General's Award in  2008 when he found out what was your  reaction honor and the wildermann  diagnosed with an aggressive form of  brain cancer Gord addressed his  impending mortality and one of his final  sit-down interviews with CBC's Peter  Mansbridge I don't want to die cuz I  have my son's 10 that really scares me  yeah  you know obviously but the singer  remained optimistic giving me this long  kind of way to do some of these things  that I've always wanted to do including  going on the road with the hip for one  last series of shows  which all came to a close with an epic  final performance in their hometown of  Kingston Ontario Downey continued to  tour right up until his death with his  last solo release secret path which  includes a graphic novel an animated  film about the tragic death of a  twelve-year-old boy running away from a  residential school not only a talented  musician Gord spent many years  campaigning for several causes close to  his heart including indigenous rights  this past December Downey was honored at  the Assembly of First Nations where he  was made an Aboriginal brother he called  it quote the greatest day of his life  and in June Gord was recognized with one  of our nation's highest honors the Order  of Canada for its commitment to social  activism and raising awareness of  indigenous issues a visionary a legend a  true Canadian for Downey will sadly be  missed  [Music]  [Music]

